        "publication_date": "2026-11-12",
        "description": "<p>This paper develops the observer layer of Observer Patch Holography (OPH). Its hypothesis is that observers are continuing native processes of the executable carrier: each has an accessible algebra and state, retains records in a commutative public record algebra, reads them back, acts on them through record-controlled instruments and continues through checkpoints. At one finite regulator a machine-checked receipt inhabits all seven observer clauses. On finite matrix algebras, every nonnegative normalized valuation additive on coexisting effects is the Born weight of a unique density operator, every pointwise-continuous automorphism flow of a full private block is Hamiltonian, and on the regional-net interface no full matrix factor sits above a scalar overlap region. Given a registered repair law, a declared clock and energy calibration and a refinement-uniform gap family, the four laws of thermodynamics, fluctuation relations and the Landauer bound form one conditional theorem, and the mean entropy production of one repair step equals the relative entropy from its input to the repaired image. The local closure P = &phi; + &radic;&pi;/AT(P) has interval-certified unique roots for each declared map, and the global closure N = log M0(UN) reads exact public-record capacity as the independence number of a compound confusability graph; a bounded counterfamily shows that its finite base structure does not fix a unique zero. A supplied charged-scalar/Maxwell action gives first-order convergent real continuum trajectories and a self-adjoint interacting Hamiltonian on its fixed mesh, read out by exact classical record feedback.</p>",
